--[[
	RATAHUB — Premium Roblox Utility GUI  (framework + polish pass)

	Place inside a LocalScript (StarterPlayer > StarterPlayerScripts).

	This file is now a REUSABLE UI FRAMEWORK, not a hardcoded screen.
	The visual identity (theme, spacing, dimensions, tabs) is unchanged;
	the internals were refactored so RATAHUB (or anything else) can drive
	the UI purely through callbacks:

	    RATAHUB logic  ->  state / callbacks  ->  RATAHUB UI

	Public API (per window / tab):
	    RATAHUB:CreateWindow({ Title, SubTitle, Version })
	    Window:CreateTab({ Name, Icon, SubTitle })
	    Tab:CreateSection(text)
	    Tab:CreateDivider()
	    Tab:CreateParagraph({ Title, Content })                         -> handle
	    Tab:CreateLabel({ Text })  (or Tab:CreateLabel("Text"))         -> handle
	    Tab:CreateButton({ Name, Callback, Destructive })               -> handle
	    Tab:CreateToggle({ Name, Description, CurrentValue, Callback })  -> handle
	    Tab:CreateSlider({ Name, Range, Increment, CurrentValue, Suffix, Callback }) -> handle
	    Tab:CreateDropdown({ Name, Options, CurrentOption, Callback })   -> handle
	    Tab:CreateKeybind({ Name, CurrentKeybind, Callback })            -> handle
	    Tab:CreateInput({ Name, PlaceholderText, CurrentValue, Callback })-> handle
	    Tab:CreateColorPicker({ Name, Color, Callback })                -> handle
	    RATAHUB:Notify({ Title, Content, Duration })

	Every interactive control returns a handle with :Set(value) / :Get() so
	external logic can update the UI without knowing how it is drawn. A
	Rayfield-style compatibility adapter (RATAHUBAdapter) is provided at the
	bottom so existing RATAHUB/Rayfield code can forward its callbacks into
	this UI with minimal changes.

	Fully event-driven: TweenService + UserInputService only.
	No RenderStepped / Heartbeat / while loops / polling for UI.
]]

